preConditionHook:
// EL: tailedCount = 0; for kk = 0 to lookback - 1: sum high - low over the
// lookback bars ending at kk + 1, divide by lookback, and count bar kk when its
// range is at or above that mean AND AbsValue(close[kk] - open[kk]) is no more
// than bodyFractionMax of its own range.
// Both terms are inside one count on purpose: two separate count panes could be
// satisfied by two different bars, which is not the claim.
// The EL twin writes the count as an explicit loop rather than CountIF because
// the large-bar benchmark shifts with the counted bar and a function-history
// reference nested in a CountIF true-series argument is not a behaviour the
// register covers. The count is the same either way: CountIF counts bars
// 0..N-1, current-inclusive, which is this loop.
// Average recomputes fresh every bar over a price expression with real history,
// so the inner sum is a plain loop -- not the WFSafe_ rolling accumulator --
// summed newest-first, EL's Summation order, and divided by the same (int)
// bound the loop uses. Products, not quotients, for the body test: EL raises a
// runtime divide-by-zero and a zero-range bar is legal data.
// The scratch locals persist across bars, so all three are reset before use.
tailedCount = 0.0;
for (int k = 0; k < (int)lookback; ++k) {
    rangeSum = 0.0;
    for (int j = 0; j < (int)lookback; ++j) {
        rangeSum = rangeSum + (high[k + 1 + j] - low[k + 1 + j]);
    }
    avgRange = rangeSum / (int)lookback;
    if (el_ge(high[k] - low[k], avgRange)
        && el_le(std::fabs(close[k] - open[k]), bodyFractionMax * (high[k] - low[k]))) {
        tailedCount = tailedCount + 1;
    }
}
